---
import report from '../../lib/clients/wheeler-opportunity.json';
import { formatRecordedAnswer } from '../../lib/clients/wheeler-answer-format';
import '../../styles/wheeler-opportunity.css';
const dateLabel=(date:string)=>new Intl.DateTimeFormat('en-GB',{day:'numeric',month:'short',year:'numeric',timeZone:'UTC'}).format(new Date(`${date}T12:00:00Z`));
const sourcesFor=(ids:string[])=>report.sources.filter(source=>ids.includes(source.id));
const scheduledPriorities=[...report.priorities].sort((a,b)=>a.current_publication_date.localeCompare(b.current_publication_date));
const keywords=[...report.keywords].sort((a,b)=>(b.monthlySearches??-1)-(a.monthlySearches??-1)||a.keyword.localeCompare(b.keyword));
const sourceLink=(id:string)=>report.sources.find(source=>source.id===id)!;
const observations=(scenario:string)=>report.chatgpt.filter(answer=>answer.scenario_id===scenario);
const findings=[
 ['Relevant demand exists','Search estimates show interest in insurance, home hardening, designation programs and residential framing. The size of the audience connecting all these subjects has not been measured.'],
 ['The basic connection is already understood','Sampled answers often connect construction decisions with insurance and distinguish a steel frame from whole-home performance. This study does not establish widespread professional misunderstanding.'],
 ['Practical guidance is uneven','Some answers mix the future homeowners policy with claim settlement or construction-period cover. More precise wording often improves the response. Wheeler can clarify the actual decision and next step.'],
 ['Project evidence can make the difference','The sample did not supply a matched California residential quotation comparing equivalent steel and wood homes. A documented case would add more than a general insurance-saving claim.'],
 ['The subject is already covered','Official sources and construction businesses cover these subjects. Wheeler’s opportunity is a well-sourced practical resource built around project decisions, clear comparisons and documented outcomes.'],
];
---
<div class="market-opportunity">
 <header class="workspace-heading opportunity-heading"><div><h2>Can Wheeler own the conversation?</h2></div><div class="opportunity-date"><strong>Research · {dateLabel(report.date)}</strong><span>Southern California focus</span></div></header>
 <p class="opportunity-intro">The opportunity: become a trusted educational resource on <strong>wildfire-resilient construction and insurability</strong>.</p>
 <div class="opportunity-tabs" role="tablist" aria-label="Opportunity research views">{['Findings','Topics & demand','Test results'].map((label,index)=><button id={`opportunity-tab-${index}`} type="button" role="tab" aria-selected={index===0?'true':'false'} aria-controls={`opportunity-panel-${index}`} tabindex={index===0?0:-1} data-opportunity-tab={index}>{label}</button>)}</div>
 <section id="opportunity-panel-0" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="opportunity-tab-0">
  <section class="opportunity-study-summary" aria-labelledby="opportunity-study-heading"><h3 id="opportunity-study-heading">How we assessed the opportunity</h3><ul><li><strong>Search interest.</strong> Reviewed 119 California keywords to understand related demand.</li><li><strong>Existing answers.</strong> Researched 20 buyer questions using Google results, ChatGPT answers and Perplexity excerpts.</li><li><strong>Information already available.</strong> Reviewed regulator, insurer and construction sources to identify where more practical depth could help.</li><li><strong>Wheeler’s contribution.</strong> Mapped findings to the 35-topic calendar and identified where firsthand project evidence could add value.</li></ul></section>
  <section class="opportunity-recommendation"><span class="opportunity-kicker">THE RECOMMENDATION</span><h2>A credible opportunity to lead through practical evidence.</h2><p>The research supports building Wheeler into a trusted Southern California resource on wildfire-resilient construction and insurability. Existing sources already explain many basics. Wheeler can strengthen the conversation with clear project decisions, documented outcomes and precise guidance. The study does not establish that Wheeler can own the entire market.</p></section>
  <div class="opportunity-stats"><div><strong>20</strong><span>reader questions tested</span></div><div><strong>45</strong><span>AI observations captured</span><small>39 initial observations + 6 repeats</small></div><div><strong>30 / 119</strong><span>California keywords with estimates</span><small>Related terms included; do not add volumes</small></div><div><strong>22</strong><span>calendar articles mapped to research</span><small>Other calendar topics were not individually tested</small></div></div>
  <div class="opportunity-findings-layout"><section class="opportunity-findings"><h2>What the evidence says</h2>{findings.map(([title,description],index)=><article><span aria-hidden="true">0{index+1}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></div></article>)}</section><aside class="opportunity-panel opportunity-position"><span class="opportunity-kicker">THE POSITION TO BUILD</span><h2>A useful voice in a specific market</h2><p>Wheeler can aim to become a trusted Southern California resource. This study cannot establish that Wheeler can own the entire conversation or predict rankings, citations or leads.</p><h3>What would make the content distinctive?</h3><ul><li>Real design and budget decisions, with the project conditions attached.</li><li>Named insurer requirements and clearly identified premium components.</li><li>Examples showing who reviewed a decision and what evidence was needed.</li><li>A precise account of Wheeler’s supply model and the builder’s role.</li></ul><h3>What the study does not prove</h3><p>AI prompt demand, professional awareness, universal steel-home savings and future commercial returns remain unmeasured.</p></aside></div>
  <section class="opportunity-section"><div class="opportunity-section-heading"><div><h2>What to prioritize</h2><p>Priority topics shown in scheduled publication order. The dates match the calendar; this is not a traffic or revenue forecast.</p></div><a href="#publication-calendar">Open calendar ↗</a></div><div class="opportunity-table-wrap"><table class="opportunity-priorities"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Order</th><th scope="col">Article / target date</th><th scope="col">Why it matters</th></tr></thead><tbody>{scheduledPriorities.map((item,index)=><tr><td><span class="opportunity-priority-number">{index+1}</span></td><th scope="row">{item.title}<small>{dateLabel(item.current_publication_date)}</small></th><td>{item.article_id==='63066716-0d0f-458c-ba18-a702c1681c4a'?'Relevant measured interest and a practical application journey for homeowners.':item.reason}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div></section>
  <section class="opportunity-section"><h2>Other sources covering these questions</h2><p class="opportunity-section-description">These publishers compete for attention and citations on the same subjects. They are not all direct business competitors to Wheeler.</p><div class="opportunity-landscape">{[
   {title:'Rules and eligibility',description:'Regulators and insurers already explain qualification, underwriting and program terms.',ids:['S01','S03','S26']},
   {title:'Resilience standards',description:'IBHS, CAL FIRE and research publishers provide established whole-home guidance.',ids:['S06','S07','S11']},
   {title:'Local construction guidance',description:'Local firms already connect rebuilding, material choices and insurance. General summaries alone offer little distinction.',ids:['S19','S20','S23']},
   {title:'Steel and supplier comparisons',description:'Industry publishers, system providers and other suppliers already appear around the material decision.',ids:['S16','S17','S18','S35']},
  ].map(group=><article class="opportunity-panel"><h3>{group.title}</h3><p>{group.description}</p><ul>{sourcesFor(group.ids).map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.publisher} ↗</a></li>)}</ul></article>)}</div><p class="opportunity-note">A CFS-specific follow-up cited wheelersteelsupply.com. That is a separate website and does not count as a citation for getwheelersteel.com.</p></section>
  <section class="opportunity-section opportunity-panel"><h2>How this becomes an AEO strategy</h2><div class="opportunity-three-up"><div><h3>Answer one decision well</h3><p>Give the answer, explain conditions, cite the primary source and show the next practical step. Keep insurance eligibility, price and claim settlement distinct.</p></div><div><h3>Add evidence others can cite</h3><p>Use approved project examples, comparable scopes and dated insurer requirements. Make the contribution useful to homeowners and the professionals advising them.</p></div><div><h3>Measure after publication</h3><p>Confirm indexing, then review at four and eight weeks. Track repeated test questions, Search Console performance, supported citations and qualified enquiries separately.</p></div></div><p class="opportunity-note">Google’s guidance emphasizes helpful, reliable content and normal search eligibility. No special AI file or guaranteed citation follows from this research. <a href={sourceLink('S31').url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Google Search Central ↗</a></p></section>
  <details class="opportunity-method"><summary>Seven angles for the existing articles</summary><p>These are additions to planned articles, not seven more publication slots.</p>{report.extraAngles.map(item=><article><h3>{item.angle}</h3><p><strong>Where it fits:</strong> {item.placement}</p><p>{item.why}</p><p class="opportunity-note">{item.status}</p></article>)}</details>

 </section>
 <section id="opportunity-panel-1" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="opportunity-tab-1" hidden>
  <div class="opportunity-section-heading opportunity-demand-heading"><div><h2>Search demand</h2><p>Estimated monthly Google searches for the topics and related terms we researched. Use these figures to understand interest and help prioritize content.</p></div><p>California · English<br />Average monthly Google search estimates<br />October 2025–September 2026</p></div>

  <div class="opportunity-keyword-controls"><label>Find a keyword<input type="search" data-opportunity-keyword-search placeholder="Search keywords" /></label><label class="opportunity-checkbox"><input type="checkbox" data-opportunity-reported-only checked /> Show reported estimates only</label><span data-opportunity-keyword-count role="status">30 keywords</span></div>
  <div class="opportunity-table-wrap opportunity-keyword-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Keyword</th><th scope="col">Monthly searches</th><th scope="col">Relationship to study</th></tr></thead><tbody>{keywords.map(item=><tr data-opportunity-keyword={item.keyword.toLowerCase()} data-has-estimate={item.monthlySearches!==null?'true':'false'} hidden={item.monthlySearches===null}><th scope="row">{item.keyword}</th><td>{item.monthlySearches===null?'Not reported':item.monthlySearches.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td>{item.originalScenarios.length?'Original candidate phrase':'Related search term'}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div><p data-opportunity-no-keywords hidden>No keywords match this search.</p>
  <section class="opportunity-section"><div class="opportunity-section-heading"><div><h2>Reader questions &amp; content opportunities</h2><p>One tested question can inform more than one article. The complete calendar includes additional specialist topics.</p></div></div><div class="opportunity-topic-controls"><label>Find a topic<input type="search" data-opportunity-topic-search placeholder="Search questions or findings" /></label><label>Editorial priority<select data-opportunity-priority><option value="all">All priorities</option><option value="P1">P1 · First emphasis</option><option value="P2">P2 · Supporting coverage</option><option value="P3">P3 · Later or narrower</option></select></label><span data-opportunity-topic-count role="status">20 questions</span></div><div class="opportunity-topic-list">{report.topics.map(topic=><article class="opportunity-topic" data-opportunity-topic={`${topic.reader_question} ${topic.family} ${topic.finding}`.toLowerCase()} data-opportunity-topic-priority={topic.priority}><header><span class:list={['opportunity-priority-tag',topic.priority.toLowerCase()]}>{topic.priority}</span><span>{topic.family}</span><span>{topic.business_fit}</span></header><h3>{topic.reader_question}</h3><div class="opportunity-topic-columns"><div><h4>What the test found</h4><p>{topic.finding}</p></div><div><h4>What Wheeler can add</h4>{topic.briefCoverage.length > 0 && topic.briefCoverage.every(article => ['brief updated', 'already covered; unchanged'].includes(article.status)) && <span class="opportunity-brief-status" title="Confirmed in the 20 October brief update. Includes guidance already covered by the existing briefs; this does not mean the article has been written.">Already added to brief</span>}<p>{topic.proposed_article_value}</p></div></div><details><summary>Search context, planned articles &amp; sources</summary><p><strong>Existing coverage:</strong> {topic.answer_coverage}</p><h4>Original candidate phrases</h4><ul>{topic.demand.original_candidates.map(keyword=><li>{keyword.keyword} <strong>{keyword.average_monthly_searches===null?'· Not reported':`· ${keyword.average_monthly_searches} / month`}</strong></li>)}</ul>{topic.demand.related_anchors.length>0&&<><h4>Related terms · context only</h4><ul>{topic.demand.related_anchors.map(keyword=><li>{keyword.keyword} <strong>· {keyword.average_monthly_searches===null?'Not reported':`${keyword.average_monthly_searches} / month`}</strong></li>)}</ul></>}<h4>Mapped calendar articles</h4><ul>{topic.calendar_articles.map(article=><li>{article.title} · {dateLabel(article.publication_date)}</li>)}</ul><h4>Supporting sources</h4><ul>{sourcesFor(topic.source_ids).map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.publisher}: {source.title} ↗</a></li>)}</ul></details></article>)}</div><p data-opportunity-no-topics hidden>No topics match these filters.</p></section>
  <div class="opportunity-demand-note"><strong>3 of 60 original candidate phrases returned an estimate.</strong><p>Broader related terms provide context. They do not measure the exact article audience or AI prompt demand. Missing estimates mean “not reported”, not zero. Overlapping variants and markets must not be added.</p></div>
 </section>
 <section id="opportunity-panel-2" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="opportunity-tab-2" hidden>
  <h2>What was tested</h2><p class="opportunity-section-description">Explore the questions we tested, the responses we saved and the sources they cited. Open a question to read the ChatGPT answers and the saved Perplexity excerpts.</p>
  <div class="opportunity-method-grid"><div><strong>ChatGPT</strong><p>20 initial answers, six repeats to check answer consistency and four separately labelled wording follow-ups. Saved text and citations are available below.</p><small>US / English web collection. Interactive widgets may be incomplete in saved text.</small></div><div><strong>Perplexity</strong><p>19 saved excerpts with research notes and visible citation links.</p><small>Saved excerpts and review notes, not full transcripts. Geography was not explicitly configured.</small></div><div><strong>Google</strong><p>20 main searches plus 10 successful shorter controls out of 11 attempted. AI Overviews appeared in 29 successful captures.</p><small>Los Angeles · desktop · English. This dashboard contains the study findings, not complete Google response exports.</small></div></div>

  <div class="opportunity-evidence-list">{report.topics.map(topic=>{const chat=observations(topic.scenario_id);const perplexity=report.perplexity.find(item=>item.scenario_id===topic.scenario_id&&!item.repeat);return <details class="opportunity-evidence"><summary><span><strong>{topic.family}</strong><span>{topic.reader_question}</span></span><small>{chat.length} ChatGPT {chat.length===1?'answer':'answers'}{perplexity?.status==='answer_captured'?' · Perplexity excerpt':''}</small></summary><div class="opportunity-evidence-content"><p class="opportunity-note">Saved AI responses are evidence of what the services returned. Their claims still require primary-source verification before use in an article.</p>{chat.map(answer=><details class="opportunity-answer"><summary><img src="/platforms/ai/openai.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22" />ChatGPT · {answer.repeat?'Repeat':'Initial answer'} · 20 Oct 2026</summary><div class="ai-answer-body" set:html={formatRecordedAnswer(answer.answer)} />{answer.citations.length>0&&<div class="opportunity-answer-sources"><h4>Citations captured with this answer</h4><ul>{answer.citations.map(citation=><li><a href={citation.url!} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{citation.title||new URL(citation.url!).hostname} ↗</a></li>)}</ul></div>}</details>)}{perplexity?.status==='answer_captured'&&<details class="opportunity-answer opportunity-perplexity"><summary><img src="/platforms/ai/perplexity.svg" alt="" width="22" height="22" />Perplexity · Saved excerpt · 20 Oct 2026</summary>{perplexity.quoted_excerpt&&<blockquote>{perplexity.quoted_excerpt}</blockquote>}<p><strong>Research note:</strong> {perplexity.review_summary}</p><p class="opportunity-note">Selected excerpt and visible inline citations. This is not a full transcript.</p><ul>{perplexity.visible_citation_links?.map(url=><li><a href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{new URL(url).hostname} ↗</a></li>)}</ul></details>}</div></details>;})}</div>
  <details class="opportunity-method"><summary>Four wording follow-ups · separate from the 45 observations</summary><p>These follow-ups narrowed insurance, California documentation and supplier intent. Better answers after clearer wording help distinguish a phrasing issue from an information gap.</p>{report.chatgpt.filter(item=>item.scenario_id.startsWith('X')).map(answer=><details class="opportunity-answer"><summary>{answer.question}</summary><div class="ai-answer-body" set:html={formatRecordedAnswer(answer.answer)} /></details>)}</details>
  <details class="opportunity-method"><summary>Study limits &amp; measurement boundaries</summary><ul>{report.limitations.filter(item=>!item.startsWith('Perplexity supplied')).map(item=><li>{item}</li>)}</ul></details>
  <details class="opportunity-method"><summary>Source library · {report.sources.length} reviewed pages</summary><ul class="opportunity-source-library">{report.sources.map(source=><li><a href={source.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{source.publisher}: {source.title} ↗</a><p>{source.relevance}</p></li>)}</ul></details>
 </section>
</div>
<script>import '../../lib/clients/wheeler-opportunity';</script>
